The '''Naviligo card''' ({{lang-bl|Carta Naviligo}}), is a reusable [[w:Contactless payment|contactless]] stored value [[w:Smart card|smart card]] for making [[w:electronic money|electronic payments]] in online or offline systems in the entirety of the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]]. Launched in September 2000 to collect fares for the city's [[w:Mass transit system|mass transit system]], the Naviligo card system is the third [[w:Contactless smart card|contactless smart card]] system in the world, after the Korean [[w:Upass|Upass]] and Hong Kong's [[w:Octopus card|Octopus card]], and has since grown into a widely used payment system for all public [[Concordia#Transportation|transport in Concordia]]. It has influenced the development of [[w:Oyster Card|Oyster Card]] in [[w:London|London]], [[w:Opal Card|Opal Card]] in [[w:New South Wales|New South Wales]], and many other similar systems around the world.

The Naviligo card has also grown to be used for payment in many retail shops in Castejón, including most convenience stores, supermarkets, and fast food restaurants. Other common Naviligo payment applications include parking meters, car parks, petrol stations, vending machines, fee payment at public libraries and swimming pools, and more. The cards are also commonly used for non-payment purposes, such as school attendance and access control for office buildings and housing estates.

